#: ../../../gui.md:1
msgid "Understanding the GUI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:3
msgid ""
"This guide is an introduction to the Ignition Graphical User Interface (GUI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:5
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:7
msgid ""
"Before beginning, you should have [Ignition installed](install). If you "
"installed [from source](install.md#option-3-source-installation-any-"
"platform) you will need to [source](install.md#using-the-workspace) the "
"workspace; otherwise, you're good to go!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:12
msgid "Start by getting Ignition up and running with a sample world:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:14
msgid "ign gazebo shapes.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:18
msgid ""
"`ign gazebo` will run the latest version of Ignition you have installed. You "
"can check if you have more than one version of Ignition installed by running "
"`ign gazebo --versions`. For example, if you have Blueprint and Citadel "
"installed, `--versions` might return:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:22
msgid ""
"3.0.0\n"
"2.16.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:27
msgid ""
"To ensure you're working with Blueprint, include the `--force-version` "
"directive when starting up:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:29
msgid "ign gazebo --force-version 2.16.0 shapes.sdf\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:33
msgid "GUI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:35
msgid "After running `shapes.sdf`, you should see the following screen:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:37
msgid "![shapes.sdf](img/shapes.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:37
msgid "shapes.sdf"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:39
msgid "The interface consists of several sections:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:41
msgid "The Toolbar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:43
msgid ""
"The orange toolbar along the top of the GUI contains two buttons, a file "
"menu button on the left (horizontal stripes), and a plugins button on the "
"right (vertical ellipsis)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:45
msgid ""
"The file menu button allows you to save the world to a file, save and load "
"interface configurations and customize interface style settings. An "
"interface configuration consists of the plugins you have loaded and the "
"style settings in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:48
msgid ""
"The plugins button lists all the available plugins. You can scroll down this "
"list to see all the plugins that are available for your version of Ignition. "
"When you select one, its interface will appear in the right panel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:52
msgid "The Right Panel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:54
msgid ""
"`shapes.sdf` contains three plugins that you see in the right panel upon "
"starting. At the top is the Entity Tree, followed by the Component "
"Inspector, and then Transform Control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:57
msgid ""
"Everything in a simulation is considered an \"entity.\" In `shapes.sdf`, the "
"entities listed are the ground plane, each of the shape models, and the sun."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:60
msgid ""
"Items in the list can be expanded to reveal their links, as well as "
"corresponding visuals and collisions, and joints, if they exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:62
msgid ""
"You can select entities in the simulation by clicking on their names in the "
"entity tree. You can also hold `Ctrl` and click to select multiple."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:65
msgid ""
"![Selecting multiple entities from the entity tree](img/entity_select.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:65
msgid "Selecting multiple entities from the entity tree"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:67
msgid ""
"You can also right-click on any plugin to open basic `Settings` or to "
"`Close`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:69
msgid "The Scene"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:71
msgid ""
"Within the scene is where you'll interact with your simulated world and "
"objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:73
msgid "Currently, you can navigate the scene with a mouse in several ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:75
msgid "**Left-click**: select entity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:76
msgid "**Right-click**: opens menu with options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:77
msgid "*Move to*: center the scene on an entity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:78
msgid ""
"*Follow*: choose an entity for the view to  stay centered on, whether it "
"moves or you pan around"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:79
msgid "*Remove*: erase the entity from the simulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:80
msgid "**Left-click and drag**: pan around the scene"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:81
msgid "**Right-click and drag**: zoom in and out"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:82
msgid "**Scroll wheel forward/backward**: zoom in and out"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:83
msgid "**Scroll wheel click and drag**: rotate the scene"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:85
msgid ""
"More complex methods for interacting with the entities within a scene will "
"be explained in-depth in the coming tutorials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:87
msgid "World Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:89
msgid "Along the bottom edge of the scene, you'll notice several buttons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:91
msgid "![Playback buttons](img/playback.png)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:91
msgid "Playback buttons"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:93
msgid ""
"From left to right, the options are `Play`, `Steps` and `RTF` (real time "
"factor)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:95
msgid ""
"Pressing `Play` will start the simulation. You can use the same button to "
"pause the simulation as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:98
msgid ""
"The `Steps` button allows you to step through the simulation at the rate of "
"a step size, or simulation iteration. You can customize step size by "
"hovering over the button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:101
msgid ""
"At the furthest right end of the scene, you can expand `RTF` to see not only "
"the percentage value that compares real time with sim time, but also those "
"individual values themselves, as well as iteration count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:103
msgid ""
"The function of the World Control options will become clearer once you begin "
"manipulating entities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:105
msgid "Next Up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gui.md:107
msgid ""
"Now that you're comfortable with Ignition GUI navigation and terminology, "
"let's start learning about more meaningful model interactions with the "
"[Manipulating Models](manipulating_models) tutorial."
msgstr ""
